Limit pod recovery bursts after host outages

Host recovery wakes every known pod, including detached pods that need
their git tunnels for automatic synchronization. Share a per-host budget
between background event-stream handshakes and git tunnel repair: at
most two attempts in flight, with admissions at least 250 ms apart.
Release admission before backoff and after the handshake so established
streams do not prevent other pods from recovering.

Wait for git repair admission asynchronously to avoid allocating a
thread for every disconnected pod. Keep host-loss cancellation and
independent budgets for different hosts. Cover admission, cancellation,
and concurrent event/git recovery after an SSH packet blackhole.

Retire queued repairs when recreation moves a pod to another host, and
check the admitted host again after acquiring the tunnel setup lock so
old work cannot consume a different host's connection capacity.
